{
  "_help": "One battle. at is a place on the map as fractions of its width and height: [0, 0] is the north-west corner, [1, 1] the south-east. Teams with default true (the default) are the historical force; the rest can be chosen instead before the battle. budget is the points a side may spend; leave it out to use the cost of the historical force. men gives the soldiers' names; fewer names than the team has places makes a smaller team.",
  "id": "rognan_alt",
  "order": 5,
  "title": "Rognan: what if",
  "map": "rognan",
  "minutes": 45,
  "prepMinutes": 10,
  "briefing": "WHAT IF: this did not happen. In fact the brigade was ferried across the fjord from Rognan and the Finneid line was never fought. Here the reinforcements Gubbins was gathering for Finneid came forward in time: the 2nd South Wales Borderers, fresh and fully supplied, with a second mortar, a Norwegian machine gun and mortar, and a 25-pounder troop whose signal line works. They meet the tired Irish Guards rearguard at Rognan and dig in around the village and the quay. Hold Rognan for 45 minutes; the quay counts double.",
  "alliedRole": "Defend. Three fresh South Wales Borderers sections and their company HQ, two tired Irish Guards sections, an Independent Company section, two 3-inch mortars, a Norwegian machine gun and mortar. The HQ can call the 25-pounders three times, and once over open sights. Ten minutes to dig in.",
  "germanRole": "Attack. Seven squads with two cycle squads ahead of them, the Zugtrupp and a mortar, with the mountain guns and a Stuka. The British are stronger here than they ever were: find the weak spot before the reserves arrive.",
